<h2 id="implementation-principles-structure-design-how-notifications-are-stored-the-relationship-among-name--observer--sel-etc">Implementation Principles (Structure Design, How Notifications Are Stored, the Relationship Among name &amp; observer &amp; SEL, etc.)</h2>

<p>First, the notification center structure can be roughly divided into the following classes:</p>

<ul>
  <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">NSNotification</code> The notification model: name, object, userinfo.</li>
  <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">NSNotificationCenter</code> The notification center, responsible for posting <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">NSNotification</code></li>
  <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">NSNotificationQueue</code> The notification queue, responsible for triggering at certain moments and calling the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">NSNotificationCenter</code> to <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">post</code> notifications</li>
</ul>

<p>Notifications are stored as structs in a doubly-linked list</p>

