<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">NSNotificationCenter</code> always posts synchronously. The asynchronous posting of <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">NSNotificationQueue</code> introduced here is not truly asynchronous from a thread perspective; it could be called <strong>delayed posting</strong>, since it leverages <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">runloop</code> timing to trigger.</p>

<p>If a notification is posted on an asynchronous thread, the response runs on the asynchronous thread; if posted on the main thread, the response runs on the main thread.</p>

